    <node id="MES">
      <data key="d0">MES</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">MES (Manufacturing Execution System) refers to the digitalization applications that are subject to upgrades and changes as part of the notification process.&lt;SEP&gt;MES is a division that manages functionality templates and platform licensing, ensuring that all templates are approved and meet operational standards.&lt;SEP&gt;MES stands for Manufacturing Execution Systems, which are computerized systems used to track and control manufacturing processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) are software solutions that monitor and control manufacturing processes on the shop floor, bridging the gap between enterprise and control systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) are software solutions that manage and monitor work-in-process on a factory floor, facilitating real-time data collection and analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) are software applications that manage and monitor manufacturing processes in real-time, ensuring efficiency and productivity.&lt;SEP&gt;MES refers to Manufacturing Execution Systems, which are used to manage and monitor production processes in manufacturing.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) are software solutions that manage and monitor production processes in manufacturing environments.&lt;SEP&gt;MES refers to Manufacturing Execution Systems, which require careful management and enhancement processes to maintain system integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-093dec1a70e2b742b9c9fed35c5bda50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2d11ba1cd77118f527559769a52464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f40d4414babdc26f99d5a8dd9445e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ea3c4866a070e16f8e1402c2ee6a9b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78c386239af9d97c4c5000c2ef66fc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ed577d3078c7fcd6f48adbbc3eb2b23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88775a42ff48905ca8238b3a4844cc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Assessment Proposal">
      <data key="d0">Assessment Proposal</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">The Assessment Proposal is a PowerPoint document outlining the deliverables and strategies for the DxDiscovery effort.&lt;SEP&gt;The Assessment Proposal outlines the execution strategy and cost estimate for conducting a digitalization assessment for customers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Assessment Proposal outlines the project timeline and activities involved in conducting a technology assessment for clients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8e304661cfd6124f3e9b284ba45f064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d3f4724ce763157782acd3baecf1b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ea3c4866a070e16f8e1402c2ee6a9b6</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digitalization Initiative">
      <data key="d0">Digitalization Initiative</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Digitalization Initiative refers to the comprehensive effort to enhance operations through the integration of digital technologies and methodologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digitalization Initiative refers to the efforts to implement digital technologies to improve operational efficiency and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digitalization Initiative refers to efforts aimed at improving and modernizing processes through digital solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digitalization Initiative is a project aimed at implementing digital solutions in manufacturing processes, facilitated by RoviSys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ef82bed5a61b39c5a2e6f0138253bf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61052dd00e5949c2e8f42c90dd046763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d3f4724ce763157782acd3baecf1b27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ea3c4866a070e16f8e1402c2ee6a9b6</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Customer">
      <data key="d0">Customer</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A Customer is an individual or organization that purchases goods or services from a vendor or service provider.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer refers to the individual or organization requesting documentation or services, involved in the discovery workshop process.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer refers to the entity engaging with RoviSys for the DxDiscovery effort, providing necessary stakeholders and information.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer refers to the entity or individual seeking the assessment services from RoviSys to enhance their manufacturing processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer is the entity that engages with RoviSys for digitalization initiatives and has specific expectations for the discovery effort.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer refers to individuals or organizations that engage with RoviSys to assess and improve their operational capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer is an entity that collaborates with RoviSys, providing necessary information and resources for project completion.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer refers to an entity that may have specific preferences regarding technology solutions, including a desire for cloud or SaaS options.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer refers to the business entity that seeks to implement MES solutions to improve its operational efficiency and financial outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer refers to the client or organization that engages RoviSys for digital solutions and is responsible for approving project proposals.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer is the entity seeking to establish a framework agreement with RoviSys for a multi-year initiative, concerned with budget and scope clarity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer is the recipient of services or products from the Project Team, whose needs and expectations are central to project execution.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer is the entity that engages RoviSys for technology solutions, providing requirements and expectations for project outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer is the client who provides requirements and feedback during the project execution process.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer is the entity that engages RoviSys for support, providing essential information and participating in knowledge transfer sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer is the entity receiving support from RoviSys, often involved in the maintenance contracts and support processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The customer is the entity requesting remote support and must approve all actions taken by RoviSys engineers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer is the entity requesting remote support and is involved in the approval process for changes to their systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Customer is the entity that requests remote support and modifications to their systems, collaborating with RoviSys during support sessions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-efa8bac083c0c59c353e35d6b2b41b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f40d4414babdc26f99d5a8dd9445e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61052dd00e5949c2e8f42c90dd046763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ea3c4866a070e16f8e1402c2ee6a9b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7cdd60303ffc2288c6e89a324a39fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a28b4f8b4caa7ca8e4a85b121337fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88e68cc88894226b2a33d91ae05741fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ca1f67b3aff2ecc0544fe29f0e5cac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57aa665558a17724e5760332bec68a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b15181be2b0b273f1c6c61c8371ede3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da747f3ceec4453ba07d55c8b9a6eee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a2d45a0a547f958cfeefdf6da7677a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71989d7e337f8fc28d7dd9fe97ec171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c39680fd69bd46de87d98a767a6624c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930089a1f69bb72daa22a86ca0b5e2d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f557cc3ef712922391c567244df05c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d32bc6d7be51cbc33d0c7efaf4e6deb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daea1eb8cfe8bd74c6b0ab853d03a193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b1e07cb422befdbcc6fd36547b07b7c</data>
