      <data key="d2">Infrastructure Evaluation is a process conducted to assess the existing infrastructure of a manufacturing enterprise to support digitalization initiatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure Evaluation refers to the assessment of the underlying shop floor infrastructure necessary for deploying manufacturing applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure Evaluation refers to the process of assessing the underlying shop floor infrastructure to support manufacturing applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Infrastructure Evaluation is an assessment performed to review current state constraints and support desired end-state solutions.</data>
