      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholder interview RACI items refer to specific instances where stakeholders are consulted or involved in the assessment process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-daea1eb8cfe8bd74c6b0ab853d03a193</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Business Intentions">
      <data key="d0">Business Intentions</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Business intentions are high-level goals and principles that guide initiatives and ensure alignment with organizational standards and investment returns.&lt;SEP&gt;Business intentions are strategic objectives that guide the execution of initiatives within an organization, ensuring alignment with corporate standards and goals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-daea1eb8cfe8bd74c6b0ab853d03a193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fddf1692f3e3d54e9ec43ee4ab9aff</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Generic Roles">
      <data key="d0">Generic Roles</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Generic roles are broad responsibilities defined within the RACI model that need to be translated into specific organizational roles for operational efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-daea1eb8cfe8bd74c6b0ab853d03a193</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Assessment Deliverables">
      <data key="d0">Assessment Deliverables</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Assessment deliverables are the outputs produced as a result of the assessment activities managed by RoviSys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-daea1eb8cfe8bd74c6b0ab853d03a193</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consulted Individuals">
      <data key="d0">Consulted Individuals</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Consulted individuals are those who provide input or information during the assessment process, often representing the customer's interests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-daea1eb8cfe8bd74c6b0ab853d03a193</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Business Process Scenario Definition">
      <data key="d0">Business Process Scenario Definition</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Business Process Scenario Definition is an activity that captures high-level details of processes envisioned within a manufacturing enterprise post-digitalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Business process scenario definitions capture high-level details about activities to be executed in manufacturing enterprises when digitalization is applied.&lt;SEP&gt;The Business Process Scenario Definition involves outlining the processes to be implemented as part of the project.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4916fbc7a1867b2372c62212ff631c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
