      <data key="d0">MES/MOM Initiative</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">MES/MOM Initiative involves the implementation of Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) and Manufacturing Operations Management (MOM) systems to enhance manufacturing processes and digitalization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Business Process Scenarios">
      <data key="d0">Business Process Scenarios</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Business Process Scenarios are specific situations or workflows that technology solutions are designed to address.&lt;SEP&gt;Business Process Scenarios capture the high-level details of various processes that are expected to be executed in a manufacturing enterprise after digitalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Business Process Scenarios refer to defined workflows that outline the steps and tasks necessary to achieve specific business objectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-57aa665558a17724e5760332bec68a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45ca1f67b3aff2ecc0544fe29f0e5cac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Generic Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Generic Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Generic Architecture refers to a conceptual framework that outlines the interactions between various systems in the manufacturing landscape, independent of specific technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Generic architecture outlines the interactions between systems and people in a digital environment, aiding in technology selection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3b35b16f5ace6b0f6122269577fa160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technology Selection">
      <data key="d0">Technology Selection</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Technology Selection is the process of evaluating and choosing appropriate technologies to support business objectives in manufacturing digitalization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Solution Architecture">
      <data key="d0">Solution Architecture</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Solution Architecture defines the structure and components of a system to meet specific business needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Solution Architecture provides a detailed overview of the selected digitalization solutions and how they integrate into the overall enterprise landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6ada47bebdfb0936d4c76944190b7b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
