    <node id="Stakeholders">
      <data key="d0">Stakeholders</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholders are individuals or groups that have an interest in the performance and outcomes of the Manufacturing Execution System.&lt;SEP&gt;Stakeholders are individuals or groups who have an interest in the outcomes of the digitalization initiatives and are involved in various activities and decision-making processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Stakeholders are individuals or groups who have an interest in the project's outcome and may include team members and customers.&lt;SEP&gt;Stakeholders are individuals or groups with an interest in the outcomes of system changes, including operators and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2892a84e446540025f19985d720cf7d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a718ba5ead2a28a06a5784fa6f2ccee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab2d11ba1cd77118f527559769a52464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1f46454562875f5de23d46e56265cd</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MES Division">
      <data key="d0">MES Division</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The MES Division is responsible for defining business process scenarios within manufacturing enterprises, focusing on digitalization and process efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The MES Division is responsible for implementing the SIPOC methodology to enhance business process scenarios in manufacturing.&lt;SEP&gt;The MES division focuses on genericizing core manufacturing business processes and maintaining SIPOC diagrams for customer engagements.&lt;SEP&gt;The MES Division is responsible for managing projects using Agile/SCRUM methodologies, focusing on manufacturing projects and related standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The MES Division is responsible for utilizing and creating user stories in Agile for Manufacturing projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-846cea9a9548723f6999d6e522d8bb41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f71e5a295481a80d1839f4ba2e4c08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7cdd60303ffc2288c6e89a324a39fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-298e2208d65e4784732a75d14634bc9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIPOC Methodology">
      <data key="d0">SIPOC Methodology</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">SIPOC is a methodology used for defining business process scenarios, capturing high-level details concerning various activities within an enterprise.&lt;SEP&gt;The SIPOC methodology is an industry standard used to define business processes, focusing on suppliers, inputs, processes, outputs, and consumers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-846cea9a9548723f6999d6e522d8bb41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Process Activity Diagram Template">
      <data key="d0">Process Activity Diagram Template</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">A template used as a basis for creating process activity diagrams, which outline the flow of processes within an organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Control System">
      <data key="d0">Control System</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Control systems are automated systems used in manufacturing to manage and control processes based on inputs and outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIMS">
      <data key="d0">LIMS</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">LIMS (Laboratory Information Management Systems) are software systems that manage samples, associated data, and laboratory workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;LIMS refers to Laboratory Information Management Systems, which are used to manage samples, associated data, and laboratory workflows.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52f40d4414babdc26f99d5a8dd9445e9</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digitalization">
      <data key="d0">Digitalization</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Digitalization refers to the integration of digital technologies into business processes to enhance efficiency and effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Process Control Systems">
      <data key="d0">Process Control Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Process Control Systems are systems designed to manage and regulate the processes within manufacturing environments, ensuring efficiency and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Historian">
      <data key="d0">Historian</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A historian is a system that collects and stores time-series data from industrial processes for analysis and reporting.&lt;SEP&gt;Historian systems are used to collect, store, and analyze historical data from various processes in manufacturing, aiding in decision-making and performance analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fddf1692f3e3d54e9ec43ee4ab9aff</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enterprise Systems">
      <data key="d0">Enterprise Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Enterprise Systems refer to integrated software platforms that manage core business processes across an organization, including ERP and MES systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sub-Processes">
      <data key="d0">Sub-Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Sub-Processes are smaller, individual steps within a larger process that contribute to the overall workflow in manufacturing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Arrows and Boxes">
      <data key="d0">Arrows and Boxes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Arrows and Boxes are visual elements used in diagrams to represent interactions, flows, and processes in a clear and organized manner.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Color-Coding">
      <data key="d0">Color-Coding</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Color-Coding is a method used in diagrams to highlight specific steps or interactions, making it easier to identify key elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Weigh and Dispense Sub-Process">
      <data key="d0">Weigh and Dispense Sub-Process</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Weigh and Dispense Sub-Process is a specific operation within batch processes that involves measuring and dispensing materials accurately.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Customer Project">
      <data key="d0">Customer Project</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Customer Projects refer to specific initiatives undertaken to meet the needs and requirements of clients in manufacturing.</data>
