    <node id="RAPs for MES -Development">
      <data key="d0">RAPs for MES -Development</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">RAPs for MES -Development refers to a framework or methodology for deploying manufacturing execution systems (MES) and includes various phases and activities for implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPs for MES -Development refers to the documentation and guidelines developed for the implementation and enhancement of MES systems.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPs for MES -Development refers to the project initiative focused on developing and implementing the MES system and its processes.&lt;SEP&gt;RAPs for MES -Development refers to a set of guidelines and standards for managing projects related to the MES (Manufacturing Execution System) implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-846cea9a9548723f6999d6e522d8bb41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fb30dd05d6733395e35883cf05930fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e2492cf7fdb3bf4be54e50ca31364c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ce8aa2923b09c026dd159f411698ff</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organizational Standards">
      <data key="d0">Organizational Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Organizational standards are guidelines that dictate the constraints and requirements for solutions to be considered viable, often set by IT/OT organizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05fddf1692f3e3d54e9ec43ee4ab9aff</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance refers to the need for systems to adhere to industry or regulatory standards, ensuring legal and operational integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05fddf1692f3e3d54e9ec43ee4ab9aff</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Level Goals">
      <data key="d0">High-Level Goals</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">High-level goals define the perceived benefits of a solution and establish metrics for success, often tied to return on investment (ROI).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05fddf1692f3e3d54e9ec43ee4ab9aff</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MES / MOM">
      <data key="d0">MES / MOM</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) and Manufacturing Operations Management (MOM) are systems designed to manage and monitor production processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-05fddf1692f3e3d54e9ec43ee4ab9aff</data>
