    <node id="User Stories">
      <data key="d0">User Stories</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">User Stories are brief, self-contained units of work that describe software features from the end user's perspective, focusing on the value they provide.&lt;SEP&gt;User Stories are descriptions of features from an end-user perspective, often derived from process steps in SIPOC diagrams.&lt;SEP&gt;User Stories are descriptions of features from the end-user perspective that guide the development and design process.&lt;SEP&gt;User stories are defined requirements that help clarify the scope and technical design aspects of the project.&lt;SEP&gt;User Stories are short descriptions of a feature or requirement from the perspective of an end user, guiding the development process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-093dec1a70e2b742b9c9fed35c5bda50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846cea9a9548723f6999d6e522d8bb41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f71e5a295481a80d1839f4ba2e4c08a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a28b4f8b4caa7ca8e4a85b121337fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985700d6939a1f7f1a71db6f2f1f92f3</data>
      <data key="d4">RAPs for MES - Development.pdf</data>
    </node>
